# Secret-scan pattern catalogue (T-1844).
# Format: <name><TAB><extended-regex>
# Read by agents/git/lib/secret-scan.sh. Patterns are tried in order.
#
# Two indexing axes (T-2692). Most entries below are ISSUER-INDEXED: they key
# on a marker the issuer stamps into the secret (AKIA, ghp_, sk-ant-, xox…).
# When adding one of those: prefer specific over generic (e.g. AKIA prefix over
# base64 entropy) — generic entropy checks belong in gitleaks; this catalogue is
# the always-on baseline.
#
# But some credentials carry NO issuer marker and are identifiable only by
# POSITION — chiefly a credential sitting in a URL's userinfo field. Issuer
# prefixes cannot reach that class by construction, so it gets its own entries
# at the bottom. Origin: OBS-106 — a live token lived in a tracked file for
# 7 weeks while this scan reported "tracked tree clean", because every pattern
# was issuer-indexed and the token had no issuer marker.
#
# Comments (lines starting with #) and empty lines are ignored.
Azure DevOps PAT	[a-z2-7]{52}
AWS Access Key	AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}
AWS Secret Key	aws_secret_access_key[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*[A-Za-z0-9/+=]{40}
GitHub PAT	gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}
SSH Private Key	-----BEGIN (RSA|DSA|EC|OPENSSH|PGP) PRIVATE KEY-----
JWT Bearer	eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_=-]{10,}\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_=-]{10,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_.+/=-]{10,}
Slack Token	xox[abprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}
Google API Key	AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}
Stripe Key	sk_(live|test)_[A-Za-z0-9]{24,}
Anthropic API Key	sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}
OpenAI API Key	sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{48}
URL Basic-Auth Credential	[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*://[^/[:space:]:@]+:[^/[:space:]@]+@
URL Embedded Token	[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*://[A-Za-z0-9_.~-]{16,}@
